+## Current bounded teaching audit
+
+The selected generator remains unchanged. A protected-Racket audit found a
+two-demonstration lesson that does not distinguish the intended rotated local
+motif match from a simpler count-only rule: choose the first candidate having
+the source motif's number of points, ignoring its arrangement and rotation.
+For generator seed 4, sample indices 0 and 1 fit both rules; sample index 2
+produces different query answers. Actual canonical labels for all three retained
+grids are `[[0,0,0,0,0]]`; the rival also returns that strip on both demos but
+returns `[[0,0,8,0,0]]` on the query. This is a concrete finite teaching ambiguity,
+not a claim that every lesson has this weakness.
+
+A separate independent geometry inspection of only those retained grids found
+no candidate whose full radius-three local signature equals the rotated source
+signature, while the generator's own `self_check` returned no errors on all
+three. The current self-check therefore does not certify the stated exactly-one
+matching-signature invariant. This inspection describes visible geometry and
+the reference's explicit extraction window; it does not infer the generator's
+unretained planted-match metadata. A useful next repair investigation is whether
+nearby motifs can enter another frame's extraction window despite the sampler's
+one-cell occupied-cell separation. No repair was attempted here.
+
+The reproducible script, exact canonical/rival programs, source-bound witness,
+runtime identity, report and execution log are retained in the review packet at
